  "result": "`String.prototype.trim` is implemented in `crates/kahvi-builtins/src/string/prototype_trim.rs`, and 4 of the 8 `built-ins/String/prototype/trim/` runs pass. The other 4 fail because they call `Array.prototype.toString` (2 runs) and `RegExp` (2 runs), which are not implemented, so the \"every run passes\" bar is not met. Clippy and `cargo fmt --check` are clean.\n\nI added a private `trim_string` and `TrimWhere` enum in the same file, since `TrimString` is not in `ops` yet. `trimStart`, `trimEnd`, `parseInt` and `parseFloat` will need it too, so it may be worth moving to `support/` later. Its white-space predicate duplicates the lexer's, because `kahvi-builtins` does not depend on `kahvi-parser`.\n\nBLOCKED: test262 files `built-ins/String/prototype/trim/15.5.4.20-2-34.js` need `Array.prototype.toString` and `15.5.4.20-2-49.js` needs `RegExp`; neither is implemented in the engine.",
